I swear, I thought you guys knew this in all these years about all the monkeys.

1289
00:50:32.390 --> 00:50:33.850
I actually have more.

1290
00:50:34.050 --> 00:50:35.350
I'll save it for another day.

1291
00:50:35.350 --> 00:50:36.790
I can't believe there's more.

1292
00:50:37.270 --> 00:50:38.750
I look forward to it.

1293
00:50:39.090 --> 00:50:40.390
Well, this was a tangent.

1294
00:50:41.410 --> 00:50:43.290
It's a true classic tangent.

1295
00:50:43.710 --> 00:50:45.070
Well, I've got a fact.

1296
00:50:45.450 --> 00:50:48.450
Do you want me to bring us back to the episode with a little fact?

1297
00:50:48.450 --> 00:50:50.470
I'm sure everybody wants you to bring us back.

1298
00:50:50.650 --> 00:50:53.150
Everyone listening right now is like, good Lord.

1299
00:50:53.510 --> 00:50:54.110
All right.

1300
00:50:54.210 --> 00:50:57.270
Well, listen, when Ned shows up at this bar,

1301
00:50:57.910 --> 00:51:01.110
his face is like peeling off in huge sections.

1302
00:51:01.110 --> 00:51:02.130
It's like red.

1303
00:51:02.290 --> 00:51:03.850
It's flaking off.

1304
00:51:03.950 --> 00:51:07.910
And I was really curious, how did they do this?

1305
00:51:07.990 --> 00:51:12.270
Because we know that this would have been like an elaborate makeup teSt.

1306
00:51:13.170 --> 00:51:15.290
And it also would have had to have continuity.

1307
00:51:15.530 --> 00:51:15.790
Yes.

1308
00:51:15.790 --> 00:51:19.210
Like, okay, this is the fifth hour into this face mask.

1309
00:51:19.330 --> 00:51:20.110
What does that look like?

1310
00:51:20.210 --> 00:51:20.730
And it does.

1311
00:51:20.890 --> 00:51:22.070
His face progresses.

1312
00:51:22.130 --> 00:51:23.530
It gets worse and worse.

1313
00:51:23.530 --> 00:51:28.190
So I reached out to Kelly Cantley, who put me in touch with Autumn Butler, the makeup

1314
00:51:28.190 --> 00:51:29.410
artist for this episode.

1315
00:51:29.610 --> 00:51:31.090
Thank you so much, Kelly.

1316
00:51:31.750 --> 00:51:38.810
And Autumn said this was a very fun makeup to design and that Greg Daniels had very specific

1317
00:51:38.810 --> 00:51:39.490
ideas.

1318
00:51:40.010 --> 00:51:46.810
Greg definitely did not want it to look or feel like an actual condition that somebody

1319
00:51:46.810 --> 00:51:48.210
would really have in real life.

1320
00:51:48.330 --> 00:51:53.970
He didn't want anyone to feel like they were being made fun of about any actual real life

1321
00:51:53.970 --> 00:51:55.490
problem they might be experiencing.

1322
00:51:56.470 --> 00:52:02.990
He also wanted it to feel very, as Autumn put it, charismatically comedic.

1323
00:52:02.990 --> 00:52:03.590
Hmm.

1324
00:52:04.150 --> 00:52:09.750
So Autumn said they tested this makeup for two days to find the perfect look and texture.

1325
00:52:10.290 --> 00:52:16.450
Greg really wanted it to look like a snake that was like molting and shedding in sheets

1326
00:52:16.450 --> 00:52:17.090
and layers.

1327
00:52:17.390 --> 00:52:19.330
Oh, it does look like that by the end.

1328
00:52:19.510 --> 00:52:23.410
He also wanted pieces that could be peeled away on camera.

1329
00:52:23.510 --> 00:52:30.450
So they had to create both this makeup that was on his face and also this interactive piece.

1330
00:52:30.450 --> 00:52:33.650
So Autumn said first they tried it with silicone.

1331
00:52:33.870 --> 00:52:36.730
They tried melted pieces of bald caps.

1332
00:52:36.970 --> 00:52:40.310
They tried latex strips, but nothing was giving the right feel.

1333
00:52:40.690 --> 00:52:50.330
So in the end, she created a mixture of Elmer's glue and duo eyelash glue applied to his face

1334
00:52:50.330 --> 00:52:51.790
in really thin layers.

1335
00:52:51.910 --> 00:52:57.390
And then they scrunched up his face and started peeling portions off.

1336
00:52:57.390 --> 00:53:01.210
She said it was like a total old-fashioned arts and crafts project.

1337
00:53:02.010 --> 00:53:04.710
I mean, how was his skin in real life?

1338
00:53:04.890 --> 00:53:06.030
I didn't ask her.

1339
00:53:07.690 --> 00:53:09.470
I mean, he's wearing glue.

1340
00:53:09.810 --> 00:53:17.010
But she said they also made sheets of fake skin with that same Elmer's lash glue mixture,

1341
00:53:17.010 --> 00:53:23.150
and they spread it out on wax paper, and then they let it dry, and then they would peel that off.

1342
00:53:23.150 --> 00:53:26.270
And those were the pieces that they would use.

1343
00:53:26.630 --> 00:53:29.470
Like, they would just attach it very slightly to his skin,

1344
00:53:29.470 --> 00:53:32.590
and then that would be the piece that he, like, pulled off interactively.

1345
00:53:33.610 --> 00:53:38.250
And then Eric said he remembered the test process for this whole thing.

1346
00:53:38.410 --> 00:53:39.910
He said it was very thorough.

1347
00:53:40.170 --> 00:53:45.050
He remembered Autumn from makeup, hired somebody to do the test makeup.

1348
00:53:45.970 --> 00:53:47.530
Isn't that a crazy job?

1349
00:53:47.730 --> 00:53:47.930
Yeah.

1350
00:53:47.930 --> 00:53:51.710
You get hired to just come in and let them test stuff on you.

1351
00:53:52.110 --> 00:53:53.350
I mean, yeah.

1352
00:53:53.610 --> 00:53:53.890
Yeah.

1353
00:53:54.110 --> 00:53:59.350
So anyway, Eric said that Autumn brought this guy into the writer's room.

1354
00:53:59.730 --> 00:54:04.410
He thinks it was, like, four times before Greg approved the makeup.

1355
00:54:04.870 --> 00:54:06.970
Look how much went into this one gag.

1356
00:54:07.190 --> 00:54:07.810
I know!

1357
00:54:08.110 --> 00:54:08.450
Wow.

1358
00:54:08.990 --> 00:54:10.110
Eric also said,

1359
00:54:10.270 --> 00:54:13.410
if I were Ned, I would have gone to the hospital if my skin looked like that.

1360
00:54:13.530 --> 00:54:16.370
But I understand he's just very passionate about journalism.

1361
00:54:16.370 --> 00:54:16.850
Yeah.

1362
00:54:17.130 --> 00:54:21.630
Well, we do find out that, in the end, his skin ends up looking amazing.

1363
00:54:21.630 --> 00:54:23.450
The next day, he's, like, glowing.

1364
00:54:23.790 --> 00:54:24.130
Glowing.

1365
00:54:24.130 --> 00:54:25.210
It comes around.

1366
00:54:25.550 --> 00:54:29.990
And just to keep throwing facts at you, I have a location breakdown for the Macaroni Barn.

1367
00:54:30.790 --> 00:54:36.070
First of all, there's no Macaroni Barn in Toledo, Ohio, but there is a spaghetti warehouse.

1368
00:54:37.210 --> 00:54:37.770
Coincidence?

1369
00:54:39.490 --> 00:54:40.330
Inspired by?

1370
00:54:40.850 --> 00:54:41.410
Perhaps.

1371
00:54:41.410 --> 00:54:41.610
Perhaps.

1372
00:54:42.610 --> 00:54:47.350
Eric shared that the interior and exterior of the Macaroni Barn were two different places.

1373
00:54:48.090 --> 00:54:49.110
We've done that before.

1374
00:54:49.230 --> 00:54:50.850
We did that with Poor Richard's on The Office.

1375
00:54:51.150 --> 00:54:51.290
Yep.

1376
00:54:51.810 --> 00:54:56.750
The interior of Macaroni Barn was shot at the Smokehouse next to the Universal lot.

1377
00:54:56.750 --> 00:55:07.330
And the exterior is actually a fakie front restaurant on the Universal lot right across from the high school, from Back to the Future.

1378
00:55:07.830 --> 00:55:13.390
So, if you go on the little Universal bus tour, you could see it.

1379
00:55:14.310 --> 00:55:18.750
So, the following morning, we do have this little wrap-up scene between Ken and Adam.

1380
00:55:19.510 --> 00:55:21.130
I just loved Ken in this episode.

1381
00:55:21.270 --> 00:55:22.770
I get why Eric loved writing for him.

1382
00:55:22.910 --> 00:55:24.570
Ken says, how are you feeling?

1383
00:55:24.690 --> 00:55:28.250
More importantly, did you make mad, ravenous scorpion love to your wife?

1384
00:55:28.710 --> 00:55:30.930
We find out from Adam they did it, like, three times.

1385
00:55:31.010 --> 00:55:32.690
And Ken's like, wowee, three times.

1386
00:55:32.850 --> 00:55:33.850
Big man, love that.

1387
00:55:34.470 --> 00:55:38.570
And then Adam's like, maybe they were just sugar pills, because three times is pretty standard for us.

1388
00:55:39.250 --> 00:55:41.190
I mean, no wonder he has four kids.

1389
00:55:41.190 --> 00:55:41.530
I wonder.

1390
00:55:42.150 --> 00:55:43.350
Snip, snap, Adam.

1391
00:55:43.810 --> 00:55:48.970
And then we have a little hint at maybe a romance.

1392
00:55:50.050 --> 00:55:50.810
Between who?

1393
00:55:51.410 --> 00:55:52.230
Ned and Mare.

1394
00:55:52.770 --> 00:55:58.950
He clearly thought she looked beautiful, but he was like, listen, I'm sorry if Esmeralda made you dress up like that.

1395
00:55:59.150 --> 00:56:00.990
I know that's not something you like.

1396
00:56:01.190 --> 00:56:02.350
She's like, what are you talking about?

1397
00:56:02.430 --> 00:56:03.230
I like dressing up.

1398
00:56:03.610 --> 00:56:06.950
And he was like, yeah, but, you know, you're asexual, so.

1399
00:56:07.130 --> 00:56:08.670
And she was like, why would you think that?

1400
00:56:09.010 --> 00:56:10.770
And then he's like, Esmeralda!

1401
00:56:11.450 --> 00:56:13.210
And he's so ticked off.

1402
00:56:13.330 --> 00:56:14.750
He's like, Esmeralda, you told me.

1403
00:56:14.970 --> 00:56:16.950
And Mare's like, it doesn't matter what she told you.

1404
00:56:17.250 --> 00:56:18.550
What kind of journalist are you?

1405
00:56:18.670 --> 00:56:19.590
You didn't even ask me?

1406
00:56:19.790 --> 00:56:20.790
You didn't even follow up?

1407
00:56:21.290 --> 00:56:22.910
But I mean, he's her boss.

1408
00:56:23.030 --> 00:56:25.470
How can he go to her and ask her about her sexuality?

1409
00:56:25.490 --> 00:56:26.670
He's not allowed to do that.

1410
00:56:26.730 --> 00:56:27.070
I know.

1411
00:56:27.230 --> 00:56:28.850
So it's like, I get it.

1412
00:56:28.850 --> 00:56:35.570
Like, I thought it was cool of him to be like, hey, listen, I hope that whole thing didn't put you in an uncomfortable situation.

1413
00:56:36.450 --> 00:56:44.450
In general, you shouldn't have to be, you know, flirting with men and sources in order to get, you know, a story.

1414
00:56:44.730 --> 00:56:45.370
And I just, you know.

1415
00:56:45.370 --> 00:56:46.650
He was trying to be appropriate.

1416
00:56:46.650 --> 00:56:47.190
He was.

1417
00:56:47.730 --> 00:56:49.890
Well, this episode ends with the Ned talking head.

1418
00:56:50.010 --> 00:56:51.090
He's just perplexed.

1419
00:56:51.110 --> 00:56:52.430
He's like, why is she mad at me?

1420
00:56:52.670 --> 00:56:54.050
Some people are just sensitive.

1421
00:56:54.050 --> 00:56:57.650
And then he's like, she didn't even notice how revitalized I look.

1422
00:56:59.170 --> 00:56:59.690
Exactly.

1423
00:57:00.350 --> 00:57:02.450
And that's the end of the episode, everybody.

1424
00:57:02.750 --> 00:57:07.250
Thank you to everyone who sent in their around the towns and to Darby for our chit chat.

1425
00:57:07.550 --> 00:57:07.930
Yes.

1426
00:57:08.030 --> 00:57:18.650
And also a big thank you to Eric Rahill, Kelly Cantley, Autumn Butler, Sabrina Impaciatore, and Chelsea Fry for some great behind-the-scenes nuggets on this one.

1427
00:57:18.870 --> 00:57:19.150
Great.

1428
00:57:19.270 --> 00:57:20.650
Before we go, I have something for you guys.

1429
00:57:20.890 --> 00:57:22.130
Don't say it's a monkey.

1430
00:57:22.370 --> 00:57:22.550
No.

1431
00:57:23.130 --> 00:57:23.650
Okay.

1432
00:57:24.050 --> 00:57:27.110
You guys know at the end of a Christmas carol, he opens the door and he goes, what day is today?

1433
00:57:27.170 --> 00:57:28.470
And he goes, today it's Christmas Day.

1434
00:57:28.890 --> 00:57:30.650
I wanted that to have this energy.

1435
00:57:31.010 --> 00:57:31.190
Okay.

1436
00:57:32.310 --> 00:57:33.470
Around the town.

1437
00:57:37.290 --> 00:57:38.110
Yeah, there you go.

1438
00:57:38.310 --> 00:57:38.790
Around the town.

1439
00:57:39.030 --> 00:57:39.710
Thanks, Sam.

1440
00:57:39.970 --> 00:57:40.110
Yep.

1441
00:57:40.270 --> 00:57:42.370
You were working on that while we were doing the episode.

1442
00:57:42.510 --> 00:57:43.330
Oh, I love that.

1443
00:57:43.750 --> 00:57:44.690
All right, you guys.

1444
00:57:44.830 --> 00:57:46.050
Well, we hope you have a great week.

1445
00:57:46.050 --> 00:57:47.270
We appreciate you all.

1446
00:57:47.330 --> 00:57:48.510
And we'll see you next time.

1447
00:57:48.730 --> 00:57:49.190
See you then.

